# Block-local binding does not escape its block

Verifies a binding declared inside a standalone block is not visible after the
block ends. Reading it afterwards fails with the standard unknown-binding
diagnostic before execution.

>>> source
let x: int = 10

{
    let y: int = 20
}

print(y)

<<< stdout

<<< stderr
eck: unknown binding `y` at Span { start: 48, end: 49 }

<<< exit
1
